& [Delineation]
  + semantic hemisphere remains in cantor_core: producer-plan validation process-record sealing observation compilation and independent verification
  + operational hemisphere belongs in cantor_ecosystem: fixed environment regular-file hashing and the existing audited Windows Job Object contained-child substrate
  + the join is one typed raw process observation; no shell flattening ambient executable lookup or second process primitive is permitted

& [Contract]
  + a sealed single-use permit is non-cloneable and constructible only inside this module pending a later separately governed activation seam
  + the runner revalidates the complete producer plan before any backend call then observes executable identity executes exactly once observes identity again and refuses drift
  + the contained spec fixes native executable arguments empty stdin working directory environment timeout stream caps one active process and one total process
  + a completed zero-exit non-truncated UTF-8 result becomes the exact core process record and must independently replay through observation and verification before success

& [FailureTruth]
  + pre-start executable mismatch performs no process call
  + spawn containment timeout output overflow exit stderr UTF-8 process-account or post-run executable drift is a typed runner fault and cannot become a live observation
  + mock observations remain supplied test evidence and must never be labeled EVO-X2 contact

& [ActivationLock]
  + production Windows backend code may compile but no public permit constructor CLI command or live invocation path is present in this seam
  + a later source-governed activation must bind explicit authority publication lineage executable identity and one-shot consumption before physical contact
